// North-row lot (housing frame, top-middle slot) — same dir="up"
// orientation as the Mansion: native y=0 is the far-from-road content,
// native y=HEIGHT is the gate, near the road.
//
// Source photo showed a two-house repeat with no clean per-lot seam (the
// garage/driveway sit off-center within each repeat, bleeding across any
// simple half-width split) — extracted one full, uncut copy first (both
// border tree rows, full garage, full gate), then trimmed for the same
// reason as the Mansion: too tall to fit above the road without clipping
// the house.
//
// Two passes before this one got it wrong: the first dropped the garage
// entirely and cut the fence off mid-structure (through its own
// flower-bed base); the second kept the garage and the full fence run,
// but the fence/hedge/flower-bed assembly is taller in this photo than
// the Mansion's own fence, so at matching scale it rendered visibly
// larger next door to it. This version keeps the same content as the
// second pass (most of the garage, the full house, the complete fence
// run down to its own natural end in grass) but scales the fence/hedge/
// flower-bed band down by about 25% on its own (500x174 -> 500x130,
// width unchanged) to bring it in line with the Mansion's, padded 78px
// past that so the north sidewalk's hidden zone eats only the padding.
//
// No clean full-width grass band to repeat-tile downward (trees and
// hedges run along both edges almost everywhere) — leftover depth on a
// screen tall enough to exceed the photo's own height falls back to a
// flat lawn-green fill instead (see groundFallbackColor).
export const SUBURBAN_HOUSE_LOT_GROUND_STRIP_TOP = 0;
export const SUBURBAN_HOUSE_LOT_GROUND_STRIP_HEIGHT = 1;
